<title>POLAND: Poland raises drug prices by six pct from Oct 21.</title>
<headline>Poland raises drug prices by six pct from Oct 21.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish finance ministry said in a statement on Tuesday it would raise official prices of domestically produced drugs, subsidised by the state, by six percent as of October 21.</p>
<p>The rise is the second this year -- in line with the schedule envisaged by the 1996 budget.</p>
<p>&quot;The rise will stop the cuts in production of unprofitable drugs and pave the way to reduce imports of more expensive drugs from abroad,&quot; the ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
